# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks files out with CRLF and records them that
# way, so a one-line edit can show up as a whole-file diff and a contributor on
# Linux sees every line changed. `text=auto` stores LF in the repository and
# checks out the platform's convention locally, which is what we want: the code
# is plain JavaScript and YAML, and it runs on Windows, macOS and Linux.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The bundled dictionary is a single 3.8 MB JSON line-blob. Git treats it as text
# by default and would try to diff it, which is slow and useless — and a diff
# would also be misleading, since it is generated by tools/build-dict.mjs rather
# than edited. Marking it binary keeps it out of diffs and out of merge attempts.
data/dict.json binary

# ECDICT source CSV is not committed (see .gitignore), but mark it anyway so a
# stray local copy can never be diffed by accident.
ecdict.csv binary
